OL,3,GNEWSASchool suspensions rise due to
OL,4,Abehaviour, says council
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe number of school suspensions in
OL,7,FLincolnshire has more than doubled over
OL,8,Fthe last five years, according to a
OL,9,Flocal authority.
OL,11,FLincolnshire County Council said the
OL,12,Fnumber of temporary exclusions at
OL,13,Fschools across the county has risen
OL,14,Ffrom 7,614 in 2021/22 to 16,803 in
OL,15,F2025/26.
OL,17,FKate Capel, head of service for
OL,18,Finclusion at the council, said:
OL,19,F"Persistent disruptive behaviour
OL,20,Fremains the main reason for both
OL,21,Fsuspensions and permanent exclusion".
OL,23,APub: 11-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
